senses.gloss:
Svādhyāya (‘reciting to oneself’) in the Brāhmaṇas^1 denotes
the study or repetition of the Vedic texts. The Sūtras give
rules for it in great detail. Cf. Brāhmaṇa.
1) Śatapatha Brāhmaṇa, iii. 4, 3, 6;
iv. 6, 9, 6; xi. 5, 6, 3; 7, 1, 4, 7;
Chāndogya Upaniṣad, i. 12, 1; 8, 15;
Kauṣītaki Upaniṣad, i. 1.
